[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) said one bug, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise. The desk
merged them by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and many
different subjects can describe one bug while one subject can describe two. This page counts by
what each report shows, so every problem gets its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October with two outcomes: <code>parser</code> fixed, <code>hint</code> won't fix
(booking-v3 retired). The <code>shift</code> problem had neither. It is still open, and its
reports keep coming in after #4471 closed.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

Counts follow the desk: a report is counted where the cause table files it. The `shift` row
lists the reports the desk read as a one-day move; the cause table files them under `parser`.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} {state} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the shared parser read every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. Day and month came out swapped: 7 April became 4 July. Any channel. Fixed by
  `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **`hint`**: same swap, different bug. The booking-v3 form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date
  field, so the tenant's people typed month first, and the form read it the tenant's way. Only
  form reports from tenants on booking-v3. Won't fix: the form is retired.
- **`shift`**: not a swap at all. The date lands **one day early**: Tuesday 12 May shows as
  Monday 11 May, a client in Toronto gets Monday while Lisbon gets Tuesday, an invite arrives
  before the booking was made. A date stored as midnight and shown in a zone west of it. The
  parser fix does not touch it: day and month are read right here. The desk read these right
  (`oneDayMove` in `desk-notes.json`), and the cause table still counts them under `parser`.

## What the cause table shows

The cause table on #4471 places a report by tenant and channel only. It cannot see what a body
says, so the one-day reports are only a footnote under `parser`:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- A report with a date one day early goes to the `shift` ticket. It is not a duplicate of #4471.
- A day/month swap after the parser fix is a new bug, not #4471 again.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. Place by tenant, channel and body.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
